This product includes software developed by others:

* src/dlm and src/mist contain the parts of FRIGID's dlm and mist packages (Bohde, Liu, Manjrekar,
  Lederbauer, Ji, Wang, Coley; https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.16648; Apache License 2.0) that MARLIN uses:
  the BERT cross-attention backbone and fingerprint set encoder, tokenizer and chemistry helpers, EMA and
  checkpoint utilities, and the MIST spectrum encoder with its data loading. Modules and functions MARLIN
  does not use were removed; the remaining code is unchanged apart from removed definitions and imports.
  mist/subformulae/assign_subformulae.py is MIST's subformula assignment script.
* FRIGID's dlm package is adapted from NVIDIA GenMol (https://github.com/NVIDIA-Digital-Bio/genmol,
  Apache License 2.0) and includes code from SAFE and FlashAttention; MARLIN's masked-diffusion components
  follow MDLM. Their licenses are in third_party_licenses/.
* FRIGID's mist package is adapted from MIST (https://github.com/samgoldman97/mist), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2022 Samuel Goldman; see third_party_licenses/LICENSE_MIST.
* src/marlin/dreams_adapter.py loads DreaMS (https://github.com/pluskal-lab/DreaMS), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2024 Roman Bushuiev. DreaMS itself is installed separately and not redistributed.

Model weights and data files distributed with MARLIN are licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0. The MARLIN
decoder checkpoints are fine-tuned from the FRIGID decoder checkpoint (CC BY-NC 4.0,
https://zenodo.org/records/19685145). The DreaMS fingerprint encoder is fine-tuned from the
DreaMS weights (CC BY 4.0, https://zenodo.org/records/10997887). NPLIB1 is distributed by MIST
(https://zenodo.org/record/8316682) and is not redistributed here.
